{
  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS001320",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates for hypertension are present (e.g., PGS000706, PGS000957/PGS000958, PGS001320, PGS001838, PGS002047, PGS004234/PGS004236, PGS004934, etc.). Among these, PGS001320 is the most supported from the visible evidence because it is an exact phenotype match (trait_efo=hypertension; phenotyping_reported=Hypertension) and it reports PRS-comparable metrics (PGS AUROC (no covariates)=0.62908; PGS R2 (no covariates)=0.06493) plus incremental AUROC (0.04424), enabling clearer assessment of PRS contribution than most other direct-match models that only report full-model AUROC or partial correlation. A key limitation is that PGS001320 comes from a pan-trait sparse UK Biobank framework publication (\"Significant sparse polygenic risk scores across 813 traits in UK Biobank\"), which domain knowledge flags as often generalizing poorly versus disease-focused hypertension studies; additionally, several disease-focused hypertension scores exist here (e.g., PGS004234/PGS004236) but lack PRS-only metrics in the provided metadata, preventing a high-confidence selection."
}

