  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are present (pulmonary fibrosis / idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis). For the target trait “pulmonary fibrosis,” PGS001791 is preferred because it has strong endpoint fidelity to a clinically specific form (idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis), uses a genome-wide shrinkage method (PRS-CS-auto) with a very large variant set (910,439), and comes from a large multi-biobank study context with European evaluation. In contrast, PGS001030 is an exact-label match but is from a known pan-trait sparse UK Biobank framework (“across 813 traits”) with a very small variant count (51), which domain guidance flags as prone to poorer external generalization; its high full-model AUROC (0.8015) is not PRS-comparable and its PGS-only AUROC is only 0.6252. PGS004695 is also idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis but is a 23-SNP genome-wide-significant score with no PRS-comparable AUC/R2 reported (only an HR high-vs-low quintile), making it harder to compare directly. Main limitation: none of the idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis candidates provides a clearly comparable PRS-only AUROC, and the target is broader than IPF, so the choice is supported but not definitive."
}

